1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:01,760
What if the Moon crashed

2
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:02,640
into Earth?

3
00:00:03,160 --> 00:00:04,170
Not a meteor.

4
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,420
Not an asteroid.

5
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:06,280
The Moon.

6
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:09,180
Seventy-three quintillion tons of

7
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:09,510
rock

8
00:00:09,530 --> 00:00:11,200
heading straight for us.

9
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:12,280
Right now

10
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:13,520
it's sitting about two hundred

11
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:15,240
thirty-nine thousand miles away.

12
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:17,020
Let's pull it closer.

13
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:18,930
At half its current distance

14
00:00:18,950 --> 00:00:20,300
the Moon looks twice as

15
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:21,440
wide in the sky.

16
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:22,760
And its pull on our

17
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:23,430
oceans?

18
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:25,060
Eight times stronger.

19
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:26,630
High tide doesn't just come

20
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:27,300
in anymore.

21
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,640
It floods entire coastlines.

22
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:30,500
New York

23
00:00:30,520 --> 00:00:31,110
Miami

24
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:31,970
Shanghai.

25
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:32,930
Underwater

26
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:34,110
twice a day.

27
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:35,290
Keep pulling.

28
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:36,880
The Moon's gravity starts tugging

29
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,230
on the ground itself.

30
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:39,640
Earthquakes everywhere.

31
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,180
Volcanoes waking up all at

32
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:41,750
once.

33
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:42,430
Then

34
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:44,150
about eleven thousand miles out

35
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:45,650
something wild happens.

36
00:00:46,030 --> 00:00:47,350
Earth pulls so much harder

37
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:48,260
on the near side of

38
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:49,240
the Moon than the far

39
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:49,720
side

40
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:50,630
that it rips the Moon

41
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:51,320
