42
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,140
So it never actually hits

43
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,180
us in one piece.

44
00:00:54,570 --> 00:00:55,030
Instead

45
00:00:55,050 --> 00:00:56,740
it shatters into trillions of

46
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:57,530
fragments

47
00:00:57,550 --> 00:00:58,630
and forms a giant ring

48
00:00:58,650 --> 00:00:59,440
around Earth

49
00:00:59,690 --> 00:01:00,660
just like Saturn's.

50
00:01:01,130 --> 00:01:01,770
Beautiful?

51
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:02,710
Absolutely.

52
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:04,110
For a little while.

53
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,390
Because those pieces start falling.

54
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:08,340
Massive chunks rain down

55
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,660
every single day.

56
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:11,190
The sky glows red hot.

57
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:12,840
The oceans boil away.

58
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,020
The crust melts into a

59
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,250
sea of magma.

60
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:16,910
Earth becomes a planet of

61
00:01:16,930 --> 00:01:17,630
fire.

62
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,090
Nothing survives.

63
00:01:19,590 --> 00:01:20,850
And here's the crazy part.

64
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,720
Scientists think this has happened

65
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:23,330
before.

66
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:24,690
Four and a half billion

67
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:25,300
years ago

68
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,920
a Mars-sized planet slammed

69
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:27,950
into the young Earth.

70
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:28,920
And the debris from that

71
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:29,640
crash?

72
00:01:29,940 --> 00:01:31,170
That's what formed the Moon.

73
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:32,580
So the Moon was born

74
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:33,510
from a collision.

75
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:34,830
Let's just hope it never

76
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:35,480
comes home.
